        "original_id": "db11097e-c8c3-5cef-9dc8-e955c22f6bce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gotthold Schwarz, Alexandra Röseler, Hans Krell, Heike Kumlin, Martin Krumbiegel\n- Organizations: Thomanerchor, Gewandhausorchester\n- Places: Leipzig, Crailsheim, Ansbach\n- Concepts: Bass-baritone\n- Works: \"O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad\", BWV 165\n\nFacts:\n- Hans Krell is thought to have been born in Crailsheim or Ansbach and died in Leipzig.\n- Gotthold Schwarz is based in Leipzig.\n- Gotthold Schwarz started as a member of the Thomanerchor.\n- Gotthold Schwarz has conducted the Gewandhausorchester.\n- A bass-baritone is a high-lying bass or low-lying classical baritone voice type that shares certain qualities with the true baritone voice.\n- In 2003, Alexandra Röseler recorded Bach's cantata \"O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad\", BWV 165, with Gotthold Schwarz, the Thomanerchor, the Gewandhausorchester, Heike Kumlin, and Martin Krumbiegel, singing the alto part.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
